Lume GF: an option to drop video and audio until the first video keyframe, for catch-up archives that begin
mid-GOP: the sound played seconds before the picture, and the frames before the keyframe showed without their
aspect ratio (Oracle Admin, 18 Nov: BBC News' archive, first keyframe 5.76 s in, SAR 64:45).
Made against KSPlayer bdfa2da (deps/KSPlayer/REVISION) with 0001 to 0005 applied.

diff --git a/Sources/KSPlayer/AVPlayer/KSOptions.swift b/Sources/KSPlayer/AVPlayer/KSOptions.swift
index b3df891..5ccbb65 100644
--- a/Sources/KSPlayer/AVPlayer/KSOptions.swift
+++ b/Sources/KSPlayer/AVPlayer/KSOptions.swift
@@ -82,6 +82,10 @@ open class KSOptions {
     /// stream's first frame (`readNextFrame`); every frame of a stream must come back at one size, since a new size
     /// rebuilds the display layer.
     public var gfProcessFrame: ((CVPixelBuffer) -> CVPixelBuffer?)?
+    /// Lume GF: drop the stream's video and audio until its first video keyframe, so picture and sound start together
+    /// on a file that begins mid-GOP (a catch-up archive: its first keyframe can come seconds in, while the sound
+    /// plays and the picture waits, and the frames decoded before it lack the aspect ratio).
+    public var gfStartAtKeyframe = false
     public var autoRotate = true
     public var destinationDynamicRange: DynamicRange?
     public var videoAdaptable = true
